# Keep shell scripts LF-only so they run on Linux even when edited on Windows.
# Without this, a Windows checkout can give them CRLF endings and Linux fails
# with a confusing "bad interpreter" error.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Note on the binaries in prerequisite/ (rubixgoplatform, ipfs):
# these are committed normally, NOT via Git LFS. LFS bandwidth on GitHub is
# metered (1GB/month free) and 40 machines cloning ~105MB would exhaust that
# immediately, whereas ordinary git clone traffic is not metered. The binaries
# change rarely - ipfs is pinned, and rubixgoplatform only moves when the
# baseline version changes (branch testing goes through exec-update, which
# never touches prerequisite/) - so history growth stays manageable.
